  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Solve each of the following equations on the given interval:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p14-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\csc\\theta=\\sqrt{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta\\leq360^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=45^\\circ,135^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe reference angle is $45^\\circ$. Sine is positive in Quadrants I and II.\n$$\\theta=45^\\circ,135^\\circ.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{3}\\csc(90^\\circ-\\theta)=2$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta\\leq180^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=30^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin(90^\\circ-\\theta)&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe reference angle is $30^\\circ$. Cosine is positive only in Quadrant I within the given interval.\n$$\\theta=30^\\circ.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\sqrt{3}\\cot\\theta=1$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta\\leq360^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=60^\\circ,240^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cot\\theta&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\sqrt{3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe reference angle is $60^\\circ$. Tangent is positive in Quadrants I and III.\n$$\\theta=60^\\circ,240^\\circ.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta\\cot\\theta=-\\frac{1}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta\\leq360^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=120^\\circ,240^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe reference angle is $60^\\circ$. Cosine is negative in Quadrants II and III.\n$$\\theta=120^\\circ,240^\\circ.$$\nBoth values have $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$, so the original expression is defined.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$2\\sin\\theta\\csc\\theta=-\\sec\\theta\\cot\\theta$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta\\leq360^\\circ$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=210^\\circ,330^\\circ$.\n\nUse the reciprocal identities to obtain $\\sin\\theta=-\\frac{1}{2}$.",
          "worked": "The original equation requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin\\theta\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}&=-\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\2&=-\\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$\nThe reference angle is $30^\\circ$. Sine is negative in Quadrants III and IV.\n$$\\theta=210^\\circ,330^\\circ.$$\nBoth values satisfy the domain restrictions.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
